From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:10:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: HDMI 3D frame packing from a block linear
 framebuffer too

The frame packing patch of nvidia-drm takes a frame-packed frame only from
a framebuffer of DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR: it makes a surface of each eye over
the memory of the one framebuffer, the right eye from line vtotal, and in a
pitch layout any line begins at a byte offset.

NVIDIA's own EGL draws into no such buffer that can be scanned out. On an
RTX 4080 SUPER with 620.73.04 (LibreELEC Hades 1.2.3, a 1080p24 frame-packed
mode): its GBM refuses a 2048x2205 AR24 buffer of DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR for
scanout and rendering (EINVAL); the window of its EGL with that modifier is
in system memory, which has no NVKMS surface; and a dumb buffer of
nvidia-drm, which is video memory, pitch linear, imported into EGL is no
target of GL (glEGLImageTargetRenderbufferStorageOES: GL_INVALID_OPERATION,
framebuffer incomplete). So the client read every frame back and copied it
into a dumb buffer by the processor: 40.45 ms a frame on average, 45.48 ms
at most, longer than a frame of 23.976 Hz (41.7 ms).

What NVIDIA's EGL draws into and scans out is block linear. In an
uncompressed block linear layout the lines are stored in block rows of
8 << log2GobsPerBlockY lines, each pitch x that many bytes from the one
before, and the memory of a block row read from its first byte is a block
linear surface of the same pitch and block height. So a framebuffer of such
a modifier is taken too, as long as its right eye begins on a block row:
the first line at or after vtotal that begins one and lies a multiple of
1024 bytes into the framebuffer (the offset alignment of an NVKMS surface),
nv_drm_frame_packed_block_linear_row(). The client draws the right eye
there (Kodi of LibreELEC Hades: DRMStereo.h, BlockLinearRightEyeRow(),
which computes the same line), and the lines between the eyes are never
read, as before: the display hardware makes the active space of the signal
itself. Both surfaces are registered with the layout and block height of
the modifier, as nv_drm_framebuffer_init() registers the framebuffer's own.

Only uncompressed block linear modifiers of NVIDIA with a block of at most
32 GOBs (those that nvidia-drm offers) are taken, and only from the first
byte of the framebuffer's memory; any other is refused as before, and so is
a block linear framebuffer with no such block row, with the reason in the
kernel log ("Hades: HDMI 3D frame packing refused: ..."). A framebuffer of
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is taken exactly as before. NVKMS validates both
surfaces when it registers them, as before.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c | 102 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 95 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c
index cfdd828..f5cbc65 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-fb.c
@@ -358,12 +358,22 @@ struct drm_framebuffer *nv_drm_framebuffer_create(
  * right eye one starts right_eye_row lines further. The lines of the active
  * space are never read: the hardware fills that part of the signal itself.
  *
- * This is only possible if a line offset is a byte offset:
+ * This is only possible where the right eye begins at a byte offset whose
+ * memory holds its lines as those of a surface of their own:
  *
- *  - the memory layout has to be pitch. In a block linear surface the lines
- *    are stored in blocks of 8 lines or more, and the right eye does not start
- *    on a block. Without a format modifier the layout is not known here, so
- *    the framebuffer has to be created with DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
+ *  - in a pitch layout, any line: the framebuffer has to be created with
+ *    DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR (without a format modifier the layout is not known
+ *    here);
+ *
+ *  - Hades: in an uncompressed block linear layout of NVIDIA, the lines are
+ *    stored in block rows of 8 << log2GobsPerBlockY lines, each pitch x that
+ *    many bytes, and a block row read from its first byte is a block linear
+ *    surface of the same pitch and block height. The right eye then starts on
+ *    the first block row at or after line right_eye_row (the vtotal of the
+ *    mode) that NVKMS takes an offset of
+ *    (nv_drm_frame_packed_block_linear_row()), and the client draws it there.
+ *    This is the layout that NVIDIA's EGL draws into: it draws into no pitch
+ *    linear buffer that can be scanned out;
  *
  *  - a single plane, so that both eyes are described by one offset;
  *
@@ -373,6 +383,52 @@ struct drm_framebuffer *nv_drm_framebuffer_create(
  * Returns 0 and the two surfaces, which live as long as the framebuffer, or a
  * negative errno if the framebuffer cannot be scanned out that way.
  */
+
+/*
+ * Hades: whether a format modifier is an uncompressed block linear one of
+ * NVIDIA (DRM_FORMAT_MOD_NVIDIA_BLOCK_LINEAR_2D with no compression, a block of
+ * at most 32 GOBs: those that nvidia-drm offers).
+ */
+static bool nv_drm_modifier_is_plain_block_linear(uint64_t modifier)
+{
+    return ((modifier >> 56) == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_VENDOR_NVIDIA) &&
+           ((modifier & 0x10) != 0) &&
+           (((modifier >> 23) & 0x7) == 0) &&
+           ((modifier & 0xf) <= 5);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Hades: the line that the right eye begins on in an uncompressed block linear
+ * framebuffer of this modifier and pitch (in bytes): the first line at or after
+ * vtotal that begins a block row and lies a multiple of 1024 bytes into the
+ * framebuffer, the offset alignment of an NVKMS surface (nvkms-surface.c). 0
+ * where there is none. The client computes the same line to draw the right eye
+ * on (Kodi of LibreELEC Hades: DRMStereo.h, BlockLinearRightEyeRow()).
+ */
+static uint32_t nv_drm_frame_packed_block_linear_row(uint64_t modifier,
+                                                     uint32_t pitch,
+                                                     uint32_t vtotal)
+{
+    const uint32_t block_lines = 8u << (modifier & 0xf);
+    uint32_t row;
+    int step;
+
+    if ((pitch == 0) || ((pitch & 63) != 0) || (vtotal == 0)) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    row = ((vtotal + block_lines - 1) / block_lines) * block_lines;
+
+    /* (a pitch of 64 bytes or more puts every 16th line on 1024 bytes) */
+    for (step = 0; step < 64; step++, row += block_lines) {
+        if ((((uint64_t)pitch * row) & 1023) == 0) {
+            return row;
+        }
+    }
+
+    return 0;
+}
+
 int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
     struct drm_framebuffer *fb,
     uint32_t eye_height,
@@ -387,6 +443,7 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
     struct NvKmsKapiSurface *pLeftSurface, *pRightSurface;
     enum NvKmsSurfaceMemoryFormat format;
     uint64_t right_eye_offset;
+    bool block_linear = false;
     int ret = -EINVAL;
 
     /* The framebuffer has to be one that can be scanned out at all */
@@ -402,15 +459,40 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
     }
 
     if (((fb->flags & DRM_MODE_FB_MODIFIERS) == 0) ||
-        (fb->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR)) {
+        ((fb->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR) &&
+         !nv_drm_modifier_is_plain_block_linear(fb->modifier))) {
         NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
             nv_dev,
             "it needs a framebuffer created with DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR "
-            "(this one: flags 0x%x, modifier 0x%llx)",
+            "or an uncompressed block linear modifier of NVIDIA (this one: "
+            "flags 0x%x, modifier 0x%llx)",
             fb->flags, (unsigned long long)fb->modifier);
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Hades: in a block linear framebuffer the right eye begins on a block
+     * row, from the first byte of the framebuffer's memory
+     */
+    if (fb->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR) {
+        const uint32_t vtotal = right_eye_row;
+
+        right_eye_row = nv_drm_frame_packed_block_linear_row(fb->modifier,
+                                                             fb->pitches[0],
+                                                             vtotal);
+        if ((right_eye_row == 0) || (fb->offsets[0] != 0)) {
+            NV_DRM_FP_REFUSED(
+                nv_dev,
+                "in a block linear framebuffer (modifier 0x%llx, pitch %u, "
+                "at byte %u) no block row at or after line %u can begin the "
+                "right eye",
+                (unsigned long long)fb->modifier, fb->pitches[0],
+                fb->offsets[0], vtotal);
+            return -EINVAL;
+        }
+        block_linear = true;
+    }
+
     if ((fb->format->num_planes != 1) ||
         nv_drm_format_is_yuv(fb->format->format) ||
         !nv_drm_format_to_nvkms_format(fb->format->format, &format)) {
@@ -471,6 +553,12 @@ int nv_drm_framebuffer_get_frame_packed_surfaces(
     params.format = format;
     params.explicit_layout = true;
     params.layout = NvKmsSurfaceMemoryLayoutPitch;
+    if (block_linear) {
+        /* Hades: the layout and block height of the framebuffer, as
+         * nv_drm_framebuffer_init() gives them for its own surface */
+        params.layout = NvKmsSurfaceMemoryLayoutBlockLinear;
+        params.log2GobsPerBlockY = fb->modifier & 0xf;
+    }
 
     pLeftSurface = nvKms->createSurface(nv_dev->pDevice, &params);
 
